[{:db/id 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0d779a1b-dcae-59f0-822c-7860f9483ab7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0d779a1b-dcae-59f0-822c-7860f9483ab7" :question/id #uuid "0d779a1b-dcae-59f0-822c-7860f9483ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72160" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ in the first quadrant?\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ y=\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & ⟹\\,x={y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/89/899357795c6d5b81d3cb619d71493ad787645697fe1f2fcecda78c1b875f388e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{x}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{3}\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ba14fe2-fe7c-5c94-b156-885bef914d7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ba14fe2-fe7c-5c94-b156-885bef914d7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ba14fe2-fe7c-5c94-b156-885bef914d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e41d7a4-75e3-58cd-839a-7c89df99b321" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e41d7a4-75e3-58cd-839a-7c89df99b321" "answer-b32afa94-923e-5681-a943-6f823eddc017" "answer-20731cc6-c38c-5d60-ad49-b4b85b44d30a" "answer-11ecb354-bca2-5a72-b